/-!
# The moving actor and odd-prime subgroup in the original hat action

For the literal escaping Y, coprime action modulo O₂(Y) gives
K ≤ [K,J_j(R)] O₂(Y), including the larger odd-prime branch. The original
geometry puts O₂(Y) in O₂(KR), which centralizes D. Thus the hat-image
satisfies K̂ = [K̂,Ĵ], without assuming that the whole preimage K is
itself two-perfect.

Since K acts nontrivially on [D,L_R], some actual Thompson-family A has
[K,A] nontrivial on that same subgroup. This gives its original B.2.4
bound. In the larger odd-prime branch the literal K-image is a d-group
of exponent d. Hyperplane centralizer generation constructs K̂_B of
order d inside [K̂,Â], normalized and generated by Â and fixed by a
hyperplane of Â, still acting nontrivially on [D,L_R]. The kernel test
uses the image of the actual centralizer inside the original hat group.

The candidate theorem constructs this data for the same outside maximal
two-local as the previous common-action construction. The component and
cubic branches retain their constructed common chief section. The odd
actor rank bound and common chief section, controlled-index Thompson
factorization, tensor identification and final generation contradiction
remain with qt-d-1319-ff-contradiction. Earlier canonical-star and source
inputs remain with qt-d-1317-supplements and qt-d-1317-source.

Source: Aschbacher--Smith 13.1.9, printed pp.870--871, using A.1.17
and B.2.4. This module does not assert completion of source 13.1.9.
-/

public noncomputable section
